Vendored files are the unmodified upstream amalgamation.  The NaN16 port
adds nan16_vfs.c (an in-memory base VFS plus sqlite3_os_init/os_end) and
builds with:

  -DSQLITE_OS_OTHER=1
  -DSQLITE_THREADSAFE=0
  -DSQLITE_OMIT_LOAD_EXTENSION
  -DSQLITE_TEMP_STORE=3
  -DSQLITE_OMIT_WAL
  -DSQLITE_OMIT_LOCALTIME
  -DSQLITE_OMIT_DEPRECATED
  -DSQLITE_DQS=0
  -DSQLITE_OMIT_SHARED_CACHE
  -DSQLITE_MAX_MMAP_SIZE=0
  -DNDEBUG

The VFS keeps databases in named byte arrays inside the guest.  Closing and
reopening a database exercises the normal pager/schema-reload path, but the
data is not persisted across VM runs.  No SQLite field sizes or allocator
layouts are patched.
